{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"Pf1e7e555"},"owner_reference":"#3277","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"Pf1e7e555\",\"feature\":\"bookend-validator-wiring\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Wire the existing BookendValidator into dh_core/operations.py create_plan and finalize_plan so a plan with non-empty acceptance-criteria-structured and missing/malformed T0/TN bookends is rejected before it is persisted, with a clean error surface on both the MCP and CLI boundaries and an integration test that exercises the gate through operations.py.\",\"context\":\"# Plan Context \\u2014 #3277 Bookend Validator Wiring\\n\\n## Source artifacts\\n- Architecture spec: `plan/architect-bookend-validator-wiring.md` (artifact_read item_id=3277, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\") \\u2014 authoritative for call sites, control flow, exception contract, and test scope.\\n- Feature context: `plan/feature-context-bookend-validator-wiring.md` \\u2014 WHAT/WHY, risks, open questions.\\n- Backlog item #3277 Acceptance Criteria (6) and Impact Radius (16-system inventory + Ecosystem Completeness Checklist).\\n\\n## Task ID note\\nThe TN verification bookend is task **T5** \\u2014 the SAM task-ID pattern requires a digit, so a literal `TN` id is rejected at the schema boundary. `BookendValidator` keys off `bookend_type`/`is_bookend`, never the id string, so T5 is the TN bookend in every functional sense.\\n\\n## Governing principle (architect \\u00a72)\\nValidate exactly at the moment a plan-write operation would leave the plan in `state=ready`, and at no other moment. This yields two gates (`create_plan` non-empty-tasks path, `finalize_plan` actual drafting\\u2192ready transition) and excludes `append_task`, which never assigns `state` and is the repair path for a plan that failed at `finalize`.\\n\\n## Verified code anchors (re-confirmed 2026-08-29 in this worktree)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py`: `create_plan` line 202, `read_plan` line 272, `append_task` line 621, `finalize_plan` line 668. Imports at lines 73-74 (`DependencyGraph` from `sam_schema.core.dependencies`; `ConcurrentClaimUnsupportedError, PlanNotFoundError, SamError, TaskNotFoundError` from `sam_schema.core.exceptions`). `Plan`/`PlanState`/`AcceptanceCriterion` already imported from `sam_schema.core.models`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py`: `__all__` lines 10-21; `SamError` line 24, `PlanNotFoundError` line 28, `TaskValidationError` line 69.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py`: `create` except-tuple `(ValidationError, ValueError, OSError)` at line 292; `append-task` except-tuple at line 524 (DO NOT TOUCH); `finalize` except-tuple `(PlanNotFoundError, FileNotFoundError, FormatDetectionError)` at line 541.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py`: `BookendValidator` lines 276-393, five rules \\u2014 NOT modified by this plan.\\n- Test host file: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_operations_sam.py` (already builds `ContentTaskProvider(InMemoryBackend())`). Note `tests_sam/` also exists; the architect deliberately chose `tests/` for fixture reuse.\\n- pytest runs from the repo root (`pyproject.toml` `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`, `pythonpath` includes `./plugins/development-harness`; no `fail_under` coverage gate). All check-commands in this plan assume repo-root CWD.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria trace (backlog #3277 \\u2192 tasks)\\n| Backlog AC | Covered by |\\n|---|---|\\n| #1 rejection on missing/malformed bookends (create/finalize, CLI+MCP, all backends) | T1, T2, T3 |\\n| #2 correct bookends still succeed unchanged | T2, T4 (test case 2) |\\n| #3 empty acceptance-criteria-structured unaffected | T2, T4 (test case 3) |\\n| #4 Pb31107bf-shaped reproduction now caught | T4 (test cases 1 and 4) |\\n| #5 automated test through operations.py, fails before / passes after | T4 |\\n| #6 tests_sam/test_dependencies.py passes unmodified | T4 (non-regression assertion); enforced by structured criterion AC-6 |\\n\\n`append_task` is named in backlog AC #1 but is deliberately NOT gated \\u2014 architect \\u00a72/\\u00a73.5: it never assigns `state`, gating it would break the incremental build pattern from #1770 and close the repair path. Backlog AC #1's intent is satisfied because every route by which an `append_task`-built plan reaches `ready` passes through `finalize_plan`, which IS gated.\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist \\u2014 intentional exclusions (no code change required)\\n- `sam_schema/core/dependencies.py::BookendValidator` \\u2014 read-only dependency; architect \\u00a78 and feature-context Out of Scope both forbid changing its rules.\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` (`_sam_plan_create`, `_sam_plan_finalize`) \\u2014 no change: these are thin adapters that already let `SamError` subclasses propagate uncaught; FastMCP converts them to `ToolError` at the transport (architect \\u00a75).\\n- The three backends (`local_yaml.py`, `github_task.py`, `beads.py`) \\u2014 no change: the gate sits above them in `operations.py` by the single-source-of-truth constraint in the Impact Radius.\\n- `sam_schema/sam_plan.py` `append-task` command (line 524) \\u2014 no change, per the ungated-append decision.\\n- `docs/workflow-layers/*.json`, `docs/workflow-result.json`, `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `graphify-out/*` \\u2014 generated snapshots. Do NOT hand-edit. No regeneration is required by this plan because `agents/swarm-task-planner.md` is not restructured here.\\n- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md`, `agents/tn-verification-gate.md`, `agents/feature-verifier.md`, `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 pure documentation whose existing claims become *true* after this fix. No edit needed; the Impact Radius marks each as \\\"accurate, no change needed\\\".\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \\u2014 no change: