act on item #3277.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"A `T0-baseline` artifact is registered against item #3277 containing one entry per criterion-id (AC-1-exception-type, AC-2-operations-gated, AC-3-append-task-ungated, AC-4-cli-clean-exit, AC-5-integration-tests, AC-6-validator-units-unmodified) with its observed exit code and captured output.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `artifact_list(item_id=3277, artifact_type='T0-baseline')` returns the newly registered entry. 2. CoVe: re-read the registered content and confirm all six criterion-ids are present and none was silently skipped. 3. CoVe: confirm AC-3 and AC-6 were observed as PASSING at baseline \\u2014 if either failed at T0, stop and report, because the must-not-regress framing in the plan is then wrong and TN's comparison would be meaningless.\",\"context_notes\":\"All check-commands assume repository-root CWD. `uv run --locked pytest` is the project's standard invocation (see `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml`); never invoke a system python.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\",\"is_bookend\":true,\"bookend_type\":\"t0-baseline\"},{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Add BookendValidationError to sam_schema/core/exceptions.py\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T0\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T18:41:45.147363+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T22:06:51.121695+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"objective\":\"Introduce the single exception type that the operations-layer bookend gate raises, following the file's existing exception shape exactly.\",\"requirements\":\"In `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py`:\\n1. Add `class BookendValidationError(SamError)` with docstring \\\"Raised when a plan-write operation would leave bookend tasks structurally invalid.\\\"\\n2. Signature: `def __init__(self, plan_id: str, errors: list[str]) -> None`. Assign `self.plan_id = plan_id` and `self.errors = errors` (verbatim, no reformatting of the list contents), then call `super().__init__(f\\\"Plan {plan_id} failed bookend validation: {'; '.join(errors)}\\\")`.\\n3. Insert `\\\"BookendValidationError\\\"` into `__all__` (lines 10-21) in alphabetical position \\u2014 immediately after `\\\"ArtifactWriteError\\\"`.\\n4. Match the `__init__` docstring style used by `TaskValidationError` (line 69) and `PlanNotFoundError` (line 28).\",\"constraints\":\"Do not modify any other class in this file. Do not change `SamError`. Do not reformat `__all__` beyond inserting the one entry. `errors` must be stored and joined verbatim so `BookendValidator.validate()`'s human-readable strings reach the caller unchanged (architect 3.1).\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `grep -q 'class BookendValidationError(SamError)' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` succeeds.\\n2. `grep -q '\\\"BookendValidationError\\\"' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` succeeds.\\n3. From the repository root, `uv run python -c \\\"from sam_schema.core.exceptions import BookendValidationError as E; e = E('P1', ['a', 'b']); assert e.plan_id == 'P1'; assert e.errors == ['a', 'b']; assert str(e) == 'Plan P1 failed bookend validation: a; b'\\\"` exits 0.\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` and `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` are clean.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run all four acceptance-criteria commands. 2. CoVe: `git diff plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/exceptions.py` and confirm the diff touches only the new class and the one `__all__` line \\u2014 if any other line moved, revert and redo. 3. CoVe: confirm `self.errors` is the caller's list assigned directly, not a copy that was mapped, sorted, or re-worded.\",\"context_notes\":\"This is the only new type in the whole change (architect 6 \\u2014 no schema changes). T2 and T3 both import it and can run in parallel once this lands.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"},{\"id\":\"T2\",\"title\":\"Gate create_plan and finalize_plan in dh_core/operations.py with BookendValidator\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T3\"],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T18:41:45.147462+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"objective\":\"Make bookend validation a real runtime gate on the two write paths that can leave a plan in state=ready, raising before anything is persisted.\",\"requirements\":\"In `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py`:\\n\\n**Imports** \\u2014 extend line 73 `from sam_schema.core.dependencies import DependencyGraph` to also import `BookendValidator`; extend line 74 `from sam_schema.core.exceptions import ...` to also import `BookendValidationError`. `Plan`, `PlanState`, and `AcceptanceCriterion` are already imported \\u2014 add no further model imports.\\n\\n**`create_plan` (line 202)** \\u2014 insert AFTER `normalized_tasks` is fully built (after line 252) and BEFORE `backend.create_plan(...)` (line 254):\\n- If `not normalized_tasks`, skip validation entirely and fall through unchanged. This is required correctness, not an optimization: it is the incremental-build start (`create` with `tasks=[]`), and validating an empty task list would falsely reject the only conforming way to build a plan incrementally.\\n- Otherwise construct a transient, unpersisted `Plan(feature=slug, goal=goal, tasks=normalized_tasks, acceptance_criteria_structured=list(acceptance_criteria_structured or []))` \\u2014 those are the only two fields `BookendValidator.validate()` reads (dependencies.py:350,373,383).\\n- `errors = BookendValidator(transient_plan).validate()`; if `errors`, `raise BookendValidationError(slug, errors)` immediately, so `backend.create_plan(...)` is never reached and nothing is written to any backend.\\n\\n**`finalize_plan` (line 668)** \\u2014 insert BEFORE `backend.finalize_plan(plan)` (line 698):\\n- Call the existing `read_plan(backend, plan)` (same module, line 272) rather than re-implementing `Plan.model_validate`; it already raises `PlanNotFoundError` for an unresolvable plan, which is the correct pre-existing failure mode to preserve.\\n- If `current.plan.state == PlanState.READY`, skip validation and fall through unchanged \\u2014 this is the backward-compatibility mechanism (architect 4) that grandfathers every pre-existing already-ready plan and mirrors `local_yaml.py:737-738`'s own idempotent short-circuit.\\n- Otherwise `errors = BookendValidator(current.plan).validate()`; if `errors`, `raise BookendValidationError(current.plan.plan_id or plan, errors)` before the backend call, leaving the plan in `drafting` so the caller can `append_task` the missing bookends and retry.\\n\\n**Docstrings** \\u2014 add `BookendValidationError` to the `Raises:` section of both function docstrings.\",\"constraints\":\"DO NOT modify `append_task` (line 621) \\u2014 it never assigns `state`, and it is the repair path for a plan that failed at `finalize` (architect 3.5). DO NOT modify `sam_schema/core/dependencies.py`. DO NOT modify any of the three backends. DO NOT add a conditional for \\\"tasks but no structured criteria\\\" \\u2014 `BookendValidator.validate()` already no-ops in that case (dependencies.py:280-281), which is what preserves backlog AC #3. Raise the exception; do NOT return a `CreatePlanError` \\u2014 that is a different, pre-existing error convention on this same function (see the architect spec's concerns block) and conflating the two would be a bug.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified `plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `grep -q 'BookendValidator' plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` and `grep -q 'BookendValidationError' plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` both succeed.\\n2. `! awk '/^def append_task/,/^def finalize_plan/' plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py | grep -q 'BookendValidator'` succeeds \\u2014 append_task is untouched.\\n3. In `create_plan`, the `raise` statement lexically precedes the `backend.create_plan(` call; in `finalize_plan`, it lexically precedes the `backend.finalize_plan(` call.\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` and `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/dh_core/operations.py` are clean.\\n5. `uv run -q --locked pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam -q --no-cov` still passes \\u2014 in particular `test_drafting_state.py` and `test_cli_create.py`, which exercise the paths being gated.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run all five acceptance-criteria commands. 2. CoVe: re-read the `create_plan` diff and answer explicitly \\u2014 does the empty-`normalized_tasks` branch skip validation? If it validates, the incremental build pattern is broken and the change is wrong. 3. CoVe: re-read the `finalize_plan` diff and answer explicitly \\u2014 is the `PlanState.READY` short-circuit present and does it come before the `BookendValidator` call? If absent, every repeat `finalize` on a pre-existing non-compliant ready plan becomes a new failure, which this fix must not cause. 4. CoVe: confirm the transient `Plan` in `create_plan` is discarded and never passed to `backend.create_plan(...)`; the backend still constructs its own plan from the same `normalized_tasks` / `acceptance_criteria_structured` locals. 5. CoVe: `git diff --stat` shows exactly one modified file for this task.\",\"context_notes\":\"Architect 2 explains why gating only `finalize_plan` is insufficient: all three backends set `state=READY` directly from `create_plan(tasks=[...])` with a non-empty list (`local_yaml.py:373`, `github_task.py:376,488`, `beads.py:610`), which is exactly how the reproduction plan Pb31107bf was registered and is the swarm-task-planner one-shot pattern. Gating only finalize would miss backlog AC #4 entirely.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T3\",\"title\":\"Add BookendValidationError to sam_plan.py create and finalize except-tuples\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T2\"],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T18:41:45.147538+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"objective\":\"Keep the Typer CLI's clean-exit contract intact when the new gate fires, so a rejected create or finalize exits via _error() instead of an unhandled Python traceback.\",\"requirements\":\"In `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py`:\\n1. Import `BookendValidationError` from `sam_schema.core.exceptions` alongside the module's existing `PlanNotFoundError` import.\\n2. Add `BookendValidationError` to the `create` command's except-tuple at line 292 \\u2014 currently `except (ValidationError, ValueError, OSError) as exc:` \\u2014 keeping its existing `_error(str(exc))` body and exit code 1.\\n3. Add `BookendValidationError` to the `finalize` command's except-tuple at line 541 \\u2014 currently `except (PlanNotFoundError, FileNotFoundError, FormatDetectionError) as exc:` \\u2014 keeping exit code 1 (the same bucket as `PlanNotFoundError`, not the `FormatDetectionError` code-2 bucket).\",\"constraints\":\"DO NOT touch the `append-task` command's except-tuple at line 524 \\u2014 `append_task` is not gated, so `BookendValidationError` can never be raised from it. Change no other except-tuple in the file (there are 16). Do not alter any `_error()` message text or exit code. No change is needed in `sam_schema/server.py`: its `@mcp.tool` adapters already let `SamError` subclasses propagate uncaught and FastMCP converts them to `ToolError` at the transport (architect 5).\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `grep -q 'BookendValidationError' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` succeeds.\\n2. `grep -c 'BookendValidationError' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` returns 3 \\u2014 one import plus the two except-tuples.\\n3. `git diff plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` shows exactly three changed lines and does not include line 524's append-task tuple.\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` and `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/sam_plan.py` are clean.\\n5. `uv run -q --locked pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_cli.py plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_cli_create.py -q --no-cov` still passes.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run all five acceptance-criteria commands. 2. CoVe: read the diff hunk headers and confirm none of them is anywhere near the `append-task` command. 3. CoVe: confirm the `finalize` handler still passes exit code 1 for `BookendValidationError` and did not accidentally route it through the `FormatDetectionError` code-2 branch.\",\"context_notes\":\"Runs in parallel with T2 \\u2014 different file, and the exception type it references already exists after T1. The architect spec's concerns block notes a pre-existing, unrelated gap: `append-task`'s tuple also omits `TaskValidationError`, which every backend genuinely raises for duplicate task IDs. That is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE here \\u2014 do not fix it in this task; report it so a follow-up item can be raised.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"},{\"id\":\"T4\",\"title\":\"Add five bookend-enforcement integration cases to tests/test_operations_sam.py\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-pytest-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T2\",\"T3\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T18:41:45.147610+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"objective\":\"Close the integration coverage gap that made this defect invisible in CI \\u2014 prove enforcement through dh_core.operations, not against BookendValidator in isolation (backlog AC #5).\",\"requirements\":\"Append one new test class (e.g. `TestBookendEnforcement`) to `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_operations_sam.py`. Build the backend the way the file already does: `ContentTaskProvider(InMemoryBackend())` \\u2014 no filesystem, no GitHub, no beads, no new fixture. Import `create_plan`, `append_task`, `finalize_plan` from `dh_core.operations`, `BookendValidationError` from `sam_schema.core.exceptions`, and `AcceptanceCriterion` plus `BookendType` from `sam_schema.core.models` alongside the file's existing `Task`/`TaskStatus` import. Every case must call a `dh_core.operations` function; no case may call `BookendValidator` directly.\\n\\nRequired cases:\\n1. **create_plan rejects (backlog AC #1, #4)** \\u2014 `create_plan(backend, slug=..., goal=..., tasks=[<one non-bookend Task>], acceptance_criteria_structured=[<one AcceptanceCriterion>])` raises `BookendValidationError`. This is the direct Pb31